## Resolved mutable: m-cluster-via-geometry-groups

REFUTED + revealed the real cause. browser-155: setting geometry.groups to cluster ranges + three's correct VAO STILL renders spikes (groups.png), GL clean (errSillosOnly 0). So even with the correct VAO, drawing the cluster index RANGES gives spikes -> the cluster indices must be LOCAL per-cluster (firstIndices were [0,1,2,2,1,3] -- tiny) and need a per-cluster BASE VERTEX offset to address the shared vertex buffer. Drawn without baseVertex, every cluster reads vertices 0,1,2... -> all converge to the first verts = the 'polys converge on a point' spikes. The lib uses plain multiDrawElements (no baseVertex). REAL FIX: the draw needs multiDrawElementsBaseVertexBaseInstance (per-cluster baseVertex), OR the cluster index data must be made global (baseVertex folded into the indices at attach time). Confirm cluster indices are local across clusters (later clusters still small), then fix with baseVertex.